>> title: Paneer
>> category: Dressings & Dips
>> tags: indian, cheese, milk, vegetarian, component
>> counters: Curry House, The Bowl Shop
>> aka: panir, indian cottage cheese, fresh indian cheese, chhena
>> pairs-with: palak-paneer
>> servings: 12 oz
>> time: 2 hr 30 min

>> step: heat to 200°F (95°C), stirring
Heat @whole milk{1%gal}(3.8 L) and @heavy cream{1%cup}(240 mL) in a #heavy pot{} to 200°F (95°C), stirring up from the bottom so the milk does not catch.

>> step: stir in the acid, stand 15 min
Stir @lemon juice{1/3%cup}(80 mL; strained) into @&(~1)hot milk{} a spoonful at a time, take the pot off the heat and ~stand{15%min} until the curds draw together and the whey runs clear yellow-green.

>> step: drain 20 min, rinse under cold water
Drain @&(~1)curds{} in a #colander{} lined with damp cheesecloth ~drain{20%min}, running @cold water{4%cup}(950 mL) through them halfway to rinse the lemon back out.

>> step: press 1 hr flat, then chill
Press @&(~1)drained curds{} — gathered in the cloth and flattened to a slab an inch thick under a board and two cans — ~press{1%hr}, then chill it before cutting into cubes.

Press it harder for cubes that hold in a karahi and softer for the ones that go into palak.
